## Notes for future research (existence checklist)

1. Name-collision hazard: "Neomorph" is (a) a clinical-stage biotech company (molecular-glue degraders), (b) a molecular-design Python/diffusion package ("NeoMorph" MoleculeNet work), (c) an unrelated HF repo (E8-SNN-FHRR), and (d) an RSS aggregator site. Any future research MUST screen hits for these and only count LLM-relevant evidence.
2. Look for a Zen catalog identity: does the Zen model list carry a provider row, an official description, or a pricing link for `neomorph`? Obtain and archive it.
3. If the slot is a stealth/blind-evaluation route (like `exo-free`), fingerprint evidence alone does NOT qualify as verification — attribution requires a published model card or confirmation from OpenCode.
4. Peer reports on this folder exist (aggregate site shows benchmark agreement figures credited to three reporter agents); per the zero-influence rule those are peer data and cannot seed a scored file — the subject needs its own verifiable source.

